From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ninjacornix <milanvrankic@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:54:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(unix): keep piped process ends out of later children

OS.execute_with_pipe left the parent's pipe ends inheritable, so every
process started afterwards (a game run from the editor, say) held a copy
of the write end of the piped child's stdin. When the parent died, the
child never read EOF and kept running. Mark the pipe ends close-on-exec;
the new process gets its own ends through dup2, which clears the flag.

Meant for upstream: a general POSIX process fix (ADR 0092).
---
 drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp b/drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp
index 21e0abf..b3fb3a0 100644
--- a/drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp
+++ b/drivers/unix/os_unix.cpp
@@ -106,9 +106,7 @@
 #define UNIX_GET_ENTROPY
 #endif
 
-#if !defined(UNIX_GET_ENTROPY) && !defined(NO_URANDOM)
 #include <fcntl.h>
-#endif
 
 /// Clock Setup function (used by get_ticks_usec)
 static uint64_t _clock_start = 0;
@@ -754,6 +752,13 @@ Dictionary OS_Unix::execute_with_pipe(const String &p_path, const List<String> &
 		ERR_FAIL_V(ret);
 	}
 
+	// Keep every end out of processes started later: a child that inherited the write end
+	// of this process's stdin would hold it open, so it never reads EOF when we exit.
+	// The new process gets its own ends through dup2, which clears the flag.
+	for (int fd : { pipe_in[0], pipe_in[1], pipe_out[0], pipe_out[1], pipe_err[0], pipe_err[1] }) {
+		fcntl(fd, F_SETFD, fcntl(fd, F_GETFD) | FD_CLOEXEC);
+	}
+
 	// Create process.
 	pid_t pid = fork();
 	if (pid < 0) {
